# GitHub main → Railway production

- GitHub `main` is the only source of truth for app code.
- Railway production is the only user-facing deploy; it autodeploys from `main`.
- When work is ready for users (especially when they test the Railway URL), merge into `main` and push — do not leave the fix only on a feature branch or draft PR.
- After pushing `main`, confirm the Railway deploy succeeds before asking the user to retest.
- Never treat unmerged branches, local preview, or one-off Railway CLI uploads as production.
